WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.835
A $30 board that

00:00:01.647 --> 00:00:02.684
boots straight into

00:00:02.496 --> 00:00:03.286
one game

00:00:03.822 --> 00:00:05.142
Steren built Circle

00:00:04.954 --> 00:00:05.779
with a Line

00:00:05.992 --> 00:00:07.289
a standalone puzzle

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:08.409
game inspired by

00:00:08.221 --> 00:00:09.010
The Witness

00:00:09.105 --> 00:00:10.307
for Waveshare's one

00:00:10.119 --> 00:00:11.204
point eight inch

00:00:11.086 --> 00:00:13.244
ESP32 AMOLED touch

00:00:13.056 --> 00:00:13.609
board

00:00:14.134 --> 00:00:14.912
It is written

00:00:14.724 --> 00:00:15.501
in plain C

00:00:15.313 --> 00:00:16.256
on the ESP

00:00:16.092 --> 00:00:16.858
I D F

00:00:16.669 --> 00:00:17.400
framework

00:00:17.507 --> 00:00:18.733
generates its puzzles

00:00:18.544 --> 00:00:20.596
procedurally and synthesizes

00:00:20.408 --> 00:00:21.374
its own audio

00:00:21.902 --> 00:00:22.715
He says there

00:00:22.527 --> 00:00:23.718
is something genuinely

00:00:23.529 --> 00:00:24.991
incredible about holding

00:00:24.803 --> 00:00:25.876
a dedicated piece

00:00:25.687 --> 00:00:26.654
of hardware that

00:00:26.466 --> 00:00:27.444
boots straight into

00:00:27.256 --> 00:00:28.246
your personal app

00:00:28.447 --> 00:00:29.260
all for about

00:00:29.072 --> 00:00:30.121
thirty dollars

00:00:30.654 --> 00:00:31.668
Full story on

00:00:31.479 --> 00:00:32.375
the dashboard
